{{also|esquiná}}
==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|roa-opt|pt}} {{m|roa-opt|esquina}}, from {{etyl|got|pt}} {{m|got|*𐍃𐌺𐌹𐌽𐌰|tr=skina}}; see also Old High German {{m|goh|scina}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Brazil}} {{IPA|/es.ˈki.na/|lang=pt}}
* {{a|PT}} {{IPA|/ɨʃ.ˈki.nɐ/|lang=pt}}

===Noun===
{{pt-noun|f|s}}

# {{l|en|angle}} {{gloss|corner where two walls intersect}}
# {{l|en|corner}} {{gloss|of a street}}
#: {{ux|pt|A casa faz '''esquina''' com a rua República|The house is on the '''corner''' of rua República.}}
#: {{ux|pt|Natal está ao virar da '''esquina'''.|Christmas is around the '''corner'''.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|angle}} {{l|pt|canto}}, {{l|pt|ângulo}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|pt|esquinado}}
* {{l|pt|esquinar}}

----

